# Twenty provider

Manage custom roles and email-based workspace memberships through Twenty's Metadata API. Data sources read existing roles and the authenticated workspace. Workspace settings, global accounts/passwords, object/field permission rules, and CRM records are not managed.

Requires **Twenty v2.46.0 or later**. This is the supported and CI-tested minimum, not a runtime version check. The provider is not yet published to the Registry; follow [local setup and authentication](guides/authentication.md).

## Example usage

{{ tffile "examples/provider/provider.tf" }}

Supply `TWENTY_EMAIL` and `TWENTY_PASSWORD` through your secret-injection process. Omitted or null credentials and endpoint values use their environment fallbacks; explicit values take precedence, including empty strings, which fail validation.

See [custom roles](resources/role.md), [memberships](resources/workspace_member.md), and [bulk membership and recovery](guides/membership.md). Keep the automation account and an independent recovery administrator outside managed resources.

